course: dictionary
lesson: 333
title: Anime and clues from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «Many children watch anime after school.» Watch tells you anime is something you can see on a screen, and after school tells you it is for fun.
explain: Look for clues about what kind of thing a word is. «Anime and manga have their own style with big eyes and simple noses.» Style tells you anime is about how pictures look, so anime is a kind of cartoon.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Many children watch a Japanese cartoon after school" still makes sense, so you have understood anime.
fact: Anime is a style of cartoon film or TV series from Japan.
fact: Anime often has bright colours, big eyes and exciting stories.
fact: «Manga» means Japanese comics.
fact: Anime is uncountable: you say «watch anime» or «an anime series», not «two animes».
fact: In art lessons, children may draw characters in an anime style to practise.
exercise: «Anime and manga have their own style with big eyes and simple noses.» What is one feature of anime style? | Long, hairy legs | Dark grey pictures only | *Big eyes | Real photographs of people
exercise: «Many children watch anime and read manga after school.» What does manga mean? | Cartoon films from America | *Japanese comics | Japanese cooking | A type of TV remote
exercise: Which phrase uses anime correctly? | two animes | an animes film | animes are watch | *an anime series
test: In art lessons, children may draw characters in what style? | a sports style | a sleepy style | a photo style | *an anime style
test: Which word means a Japanese comic? | style | series | anime | *manga
exam: What does the word anime mean? | *A style of cartoon film or TV series from Japan | A kind of Japanese food | A type of pencil | A sport played on ice
